  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "decode_R13_R2000",
    "file": "libredwg/src/decode.c",
    "description": "The crash is an assertion-triggered abort in decode_R13_R2000 at `assert(dat->byte == 0xb)`. The function assumes the bitstream cursor is at byte 0x0b after parsing the DWG version magic, but this is only true for sufficiently sized/valid R13-R2000 inputs. With the provided malformed tiny AC1015 input, parsing in `header.spec` leaves `dat->byte` at a different position, so the hard assert fires instead of graceful validation/error handling.",
    "conditions": "Data flow: llvmfuzz passes attacker-controlled bytes directly to `dwg_decode` when input starts with 'AC'. For an R13-R2000 magic (e.g., AC1015) and a truncated/minimal malformed file that still passes initial size/magic checks, `dwg_decode` dispatches to `decode_R13_R2000`. The function reaches the invariant check `assert(dat->byte == 0xb)` and aborts when the cursor is not exactly 0x0b. Thus, this PoV is triggered by malformed AC10xx DWG data that violates this internal parser assumption."
  },
